 dozen merchant ships and  crippled trade in the bahamas when he  finally sailed back to nassau vane was  delighted to find that pierce had  departed but something else ominous soon  appeared  a hulking five-vessel fleet with  towering warships approached and laid  anchor  blackbeard was in town  his 700 strong crew found their land  legs in the taverns and brothels of  nassau and for a brief moment it looked  like the glorious pre-pardoned days of  the island had returned  blackbeard however was not keen on a  potential run-in with woods rogers and  in a few days he and his crew sailed  away  finally vane attacked benjamin hornegold  and proclaimed himself the governor of  new providence it seemed charles vane  was the last true pirate lord in this  corner of the world old allies had  turned against him henry jennings had  even accepted a privateering commission  to arrest vane but vain rich with the  spoils of his exploits now planned to  set sail for brazil with his crew where  they might regroup and build another  pirate paradise  but as they readied their ships hostile  sails appeared  woods rogers blocked vane in the harbour  this was the final chance to take the  pardon and escape  alive  all surrendered to the pardon except  charles vane and his crew which happened  after this manner the harbour had two  inlets by means of a small island lying  at the mouth of it at one of which both  the men of war entered and left the  other open so that vanes slipped his  cable set fire to a large prize they had  there and resolutely put out firing at  the man of war as he went off  despite this attack woods rogers  nevertheless became the governor of new  providence and he entrusted benjamin  hornergold with a dangerous mission to  hunt down charles vane but vane had  informants and old allies scattered  across the west indies and he shrunkly  evaded rogers and horner gold at every  turn  as charles vane persisted in a bloody  tour of piracy dozens of superficially  reformed pirates betrayed the pardon  stole ships and sailed off to join his  course  if arrested they would be tried under  maritime law and thus afforded no jury  pirate trials were little more than a  show well-promoted propaganda intended  to sear a gruesome image in the minds of  all would-be pirates without the aid of  a defense lawyer the mostly illiterate  sea thieves would be asked to prove  their innocence to a panel of appointed  officials the accused would inevitably  be found guilty hanged on the foreshore  and buried in an unmarked grave or left  to rot in a swinging cage this was the  fate the crown had now reserved for all  pirates  but charles vane pressed onwards  [Music]  while many of his old crew like edward  england and christopher condont had left  for africa and brazil one powerful  pirate still stalked american waters  vane found blackbeard in the ocracoke  inlet off the coast of north carolina  and ordered cannons fired in a salute to  his fellow pirate  as the two crews fraternized and drank  for several nights on the beach vane  likely attempted to convince blackbeard  to sail with him but blackbeard again  sailed off separately intent on staging  a few last attacks on vulnerable targets  before his own planned retirement from  piracy  only a month later in november of 1718  british lieutenant robert maynard caught  up to blackbeard and launched a surprise  attack blackbeard quickly fired back his  crew wounded or killed 21 of the british  attackers and boarded the enemy vessel  to finish the job but a dozen british  sailors lay hidden in the hold they  emerged and charged with maynard across  a deck sleek with blood in a haze of  musket fire the giant blackbeard  appeared and lunged at the rival captain  maynard locked swords with blackbeard  swinging furiously the pair dueled until  at last maynard struck his challenger  the enormous pirate shattered the sword  lodged inside of him and reached for his  pistol but again maynard was quicker and  shot him  here was an end of that courageous brute  who might have passed in the world for a  hero had he been employed in good cause  the lieutenant caused blackbeard's head  to be severed from his body and hung up  at the bold spirit end then he sailed to  bathtown to get relief for his wounded  men  it might have seemed prudent for charles  vane to avoid a similar fate and he  retreated when a french naval ship fired  on him just a day later but his crew  took his caution for cowardice in  accordance with the pirate code the crew  exercised their right to vote him out  his shipmate calico jack rackham took  the helm and with a small gang of loyal  supporters charles vane was sent off in  a mega sloop he continued to attack and  rob merchant vessels but soon a dark  storm descended upon his ship the small  vessel screeched and teetered over  thunderous swells vane and the crew were  thrashed about the deck until the waves  overtook them their plunder was lost and  the crew was thrown  overboard  and yet  this wasn't  the end  among the drifting wreckage that washed  up on the still shores of a desert  island was splintered wood strips of  sail and the captain himself charles  vane  the castaway had cheated death he  crawled ashore through clumped sand and  cursed his wretched lot here on some  unknown stretch of land vane languished  days passed under a beating sun he spent  his hours gazing out at a desolate  blue-green horizon seeing not another  soul at last a group of turtle hunters  stopped by to find a stinking and hungry  child's vein dressed in weather-worn  clothes they provided the miserable  pirate with turtle flesh to sustain  himself and continued on their way  vane remained brooding on the island for  weeks until in early 1719 he spotted his  saving opportunity an english vessel  from jamaica stopped on the island vane  happened to be an old acquaintance of  its commander captain halford but  holford was a retired buccaneer who knew  vane well enough to bar the conniving  pirate from boarding still some part of  hulford took pity on the castaway rather  than a rest vane outright hulford gave  his old friend a running start  i am now going down the bay and shall  return hither in about a month if i find  you upon the island when i come back  i'll carry you to jamaica and hang you  holford sailed off and vane was left to  scour the horizon for a rescuer within a  few days another english ship arrived  the sailors met the weary castaway and  heard his sympathetic plight vane gave  them a false name and joined their crew  they began to sail out of the bay  one would be apt to think that vane was  now pretty safe and likely to escape the  fate which his crimes had merited but  here a cross accident happened that  ruined all holford returning from the  bay was met by this ship the captains  being very well acquainted together  holford was invited to dine and as he  passed along to the cabin he chanced to  cast his eye down the hold and there saw  charles vane at work  holford arrested vane at gunpoint and  carried the chained pirate back to  jamaica there authorities finally locked  him in a cell  the anti-piracy efforts of the crown had  worked well in short order the last of  the great pirates would disappear  including those who had fled eastward  pardoned men like henry jennings could  retire in domesticity the thousands who  refused the king's offer were hunted  down and hanged  others lost their lives on the high seas  some would be dashed against rocks in  hurricanes the great bartholomew roberts  was shot in the throat and still others  like the brutal edward lowe who  notoriously forced a man to eat his own  broiled lips  disappeared  though likely captured and killed a  wishful caribbean criminal might imagine  missing pirates like lowe and henry  every had made it out alive  that they had cheated the hangman and  lived out the rest of their days sipping  rum amidst their plunder  as for charles vane a 